sieve-filter-v1
; An example of `requires`: its own rule is small (no word longer than longest letters), and it
; switches on clean-data-v1 and max-run-data-v1 (at max=3) with it, so ticking it ticks a tidy
; stack in one go. Its own settings and the ones it pins are all adjustable.
id        tidy-data
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     text
symbols   lower27
describe  No word longer than longest letters, and it switches on clean-data-v1 and max-run-data-v1 (max 3) with it.
requires  clean-data-v1
requires  max-run-data-v1  max=3
param     longest  int  20  1  200  longest word allowed, in letters

class     space   " "
class     letter  a-z

; state k: the current word has k letters so far
states    {longest + 1}
start     0
accept    0..{longest}
for k 0 longest
  t   {k}   space   0
done
for k 0 {longest - 1}
  t   {k}   letter  {k + 1}
done
end
